# Copy this file to .env.local (for local development) and fill in your values.
# IMPORTANT: Never commit real secrets. .env.local is gitignored.

# Get your API key from https://resend.com/api-keys
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# NOTES FOR CONTACT FORM TO WORK:
# 1. The contact form uses Resend to send emails to info@højfynsspartel.dk
# 2. By default (without verified domain) you can ONLY send emails TO the email
#    address you used when you signed up for Resend.
# 3. To send to info@højfynsspartel.dk (and have it look professional):
#    - Go to https://resend.com/domains
#    - Add and verify your domain (højfynsspartel.dk recommended, or use a subdomain)
#    - Add the required DNS records (DKIM + SPF)
#    - Once verified, the from address in app/api/contact/route.ts will work
#      (currently set to info@højfynsspartel.dk)
# 4. QUICK TEST WITHOUT DOMAIN VERIFICATION (only for testing the form flow):
#    - Temporarily edit app/api/contact/route.ts :
#        from: 'onboarding@resend.dev',
#        to: ['din-egen-resend-signup@email.dk'],   // must be exactly the email you used to create the Resend account
#    - Then the email will arrive in your inbox (from Resend test).
#    - Remember to revert + verify domain before going live.
# 5. After setting .env.local or changing env vars, restart `npm run dev`.
# 6. In production (e.g. Vercel), add RESEND_API_KEY under Project Settings > Environment Variables (Production + Preview).

# Optional: you can also set this in your hosting platform (Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables)
